<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαίθαργος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, said
		to mean <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>biting secretly</i>
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαθεῖν, δάκνω</span>), i.e. without
			barking, of a dog, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαίνεις δάκνουσα καὶ κύων λ. εἶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					885
				</span></i>
			, cf. Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1068
			</span></i>; also, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαθραῖος, λαιθάργῳ
				ποδί</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
				227
			</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάθαργος</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				<u>PS</u>
				p.87
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λήθαργος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
